  {
    "why": "sevdesk-mcp supports only bookkeeping system 2.0, yet the document models require fields sevDesk's own descriptions rule out there: taxType ('Use this in sevdesk-Update 1.0 (instead of taxRule)'), the document-level taxRate ('This is not used anymore. Use the taxRate of the individual positions instead.'), addressCountry ('Can be omitted as complete address is defined in address attribute') and, for voucher positions, accountingType (accountDatev: 'Use this in sevdesk-Update 2.0 (replaces accountingType)'). The order model also misses orderType, which the Order docs mark as necessary ('you will need to provide the order type when creating an order').",
    "changes": [
      {
        "path": "/components/schemas/Model_Order/required",
        "from": [
          "orderNumber",
          "orderDate",
          "contact",
          "status",
          "addressCountry",
          "contactPerson",
          "taxRate",
          "taxRule",
          "taxText",
          "taxType",
          "currency",
          "header",
          "version",
          "mapAll"
        ],
        "to": [
          "orderNumber",
          "orderDate",
          "contact",
          "status",
          "contactPerson",
          "taxRule",
          "taxText",
          "currency",
          "header",
          "version",
          "mapAll",
          "orderType"
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "/components/schemas/Model_Invoice/required",
        "from": [
          "invoiceDate",
          "contact",
          "discount",
          "status",
          "addressCountry",
          "contactPerson",
          "taxRate",
          "taxRule",
          "taxText",
          "taxType",
          "invoiceType",
          "currency",
          "mapAll"
        ],
        "to": [
          "invoiceDate",
          "contact",
          "discount",
          "status",
          "contactPerson",
          "taxRule",
          "taxText",
          "invoiceType",
          "currency",
          "mapAll"
